Stop closed HTTP/2 client connections from being retained by their timers.

Source: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/http/pull/2
Pinned revision: 6a8cb5e86620ff368c58bc7ace9a5622b513098a

Retain the PR's fixes in both the bundled and standalone HTTP/2 clients and its
original connection-retention regression test. Add source-reference comments
and deterministic checks in both clients: completing the last stream must arm
the idle timer on an open connection and leave it stopped on a closed one.
A closed connection has no use for a timer keeping its buffers as souvenirs.

